          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p></p><p>We are committed to the quality and craftsmanship of our rugs. All Imperial Knots rugs include a <strong>6-month warranty</strong> from the date of delivery against <strong>manufacturing defects</strong>.</p><p><strong>What’s Covered</strong></p><p>This warranty covers defects in:</p><ul><li>Weaving or construction</li><li>Materials or workmanship</li><li>Issues<a href=\"https://www.imperialknots.com/?_ab=0&_fd=0&_sc=1&preview_theme_id=182488662323\" target=\"_blank\">Preview</a> that impact the rug’s structure, durability, or appearance</li></ul><p>The warranty applies only to the <strong>original purchaser</strong> and is <strong>non-transferable</strong>.</p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>What’s Not Covered (Exclusions)</strong></p><p>This warranty does <strong>not</strong> cover damage or changes that occur as part of normal use or natural characteristics of handcrafted rugs.</p><p><strong>Normal characteristics (not defects):</strong></p><ul><li>Natural fiber slubs or texture variation</li><li>Minor weaving variances</li><li>Loose yarn ends (“sprouting”)</li><li>Initial shedding</li><li>Light packaging odour</li><li>Temporary fold/crease marks</li><li>Size variation up to <strong>±3%</strong></li><li>Colour variation due to natural dye lots</li></ul><p><strong>Wear & use over time:</strong></p><ul><li>Normal wear and tear</li><li>Pile crushing or flattening</li><li>Shading, watermarking, or texture change</li><li>Fringe variations</li><li>Sunlight/UV colour fading</li></ul><p><strong>Damage from use or environment:</strong></p><ul><li>Stains and spills</li><li>Pet-related damage</li><li>Snags, pulls, burns</li><li>Moth/insect damage</li><li>Mold/mildew</li><li>Water/chemical exposure</li><li>Improper or harsh cleaning methods</li></ul><p><strong>Improper placement or handling:</strong></p><ul><li>Use <strong>without a rug pad</strong> on hard floors</li><li>Cutting, trimming, or altering the rug</li><li>Use in <strong>commercial/high-traffic</strong> settings if the rug is rated for residential use</li><li>Damage from heavy furniture without protective pads/casters</li></ul><p><strong>Third-party or storage damage:</strong></p><ul><li>Repairs or cleaning by non-approved providers</li><li>Damage that occurs during storage after delivery</li></ul><p><strong>Transit damage:</strong></p><ul><li>Must be reported <strong>within 48 hours of delivery</strong>; claims outside this window are not covered.</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p><strong>How to Report a Concern</strong></p><p>If you believe your rug has a manufacturing defect:</p><ol><li>Email <strong>customercare@imperialknots.com</strong> or call <strong>+91-95591-40222</strong></li><li>Provide your <strong>order number</strong></li><li>Share:</li></ol><ul><li>At least 3-<strong>4 clear photos</strong> showing the rug and the concern</li><li>A short <strong>video</strong> if the issue is structural or movement-related</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p><strong>What Happens Next</strong></p><ul><li>We review the issue and may request further details or schedule an inspection.</li><li>If the defect is covered, we will <strong>repair, replace, or refund</strong> the rug based on what we determine is the most suitable solution.</li><li>If a replacement is issued, the warranty continues from the <strong>original delivery date</strong>, not renewed.</li></ul><p><strong>Shipping for Inspection</strong></p><ul><li>The customer initially covers shipping for return evaluation.</li><li>If a manufacturing defect is confirmed, <strong>we will reimburse or arrange pickup</strong>.</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p><strong>Policy Updates</strong></p><p>Imperial Knots may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be available through our customer support team or on our website.</p>"
          }
